<title>SWEDEN: Electrolux Q1 profit falls 14 pct.</title>
<headline>Electrolux Q1 profit falls 14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish appliance maker Electrolux on Tuesday presented earnings for the three months to March 31, 1997,</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		  777   vs     901</p>
<p> Sales				    28,715   vs  27,582</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			    694   vs     797</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				5.70  vs    6.90</p>
<p> Operating costs			27,599   vs  26,426</p>
<p> Depreciation			    1,184   vs   1,134</p>
<p> Operating profit			1,116   vs   1,156</p>
<p> Net financial items		     339   vs     255</p>
<p> Minorities				   83   vs     104</p>
<p> Taxes					 278   vs     295</p>
<p>NOTE -- Swedish Electrolux AB is a household applicance manufacturer. Analysts polled by Reuters said they expected the company to post a profit of 910 million crowns on average.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
